examples.question_text:
The scatterplot shows advertising spend $A$, in thousands of dollars, and sales $S$, in thousands of dollars. A line of best fit is drawn.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.11cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{fitcolour}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\draw[gridcolour,xstep=1,ystep=10] (0,0) grid (10,60);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.7,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,64);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {10,20,30,40,50,60} {\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\path (5,-9) node {Advertising spend ($\$1000$)};
\path (-1.5,30) node[rotate=90] {Sales ($\$1000$)};
\foreach \x/\y in {0/12,1/11,2/20,3/19,4/28,5/27,6/36,7/35,8/44,10/48} {\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (1.8pt);}
\draw[fitcolour,thick] (0,10)--(10,50);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Find the gradient and interpret it.
b. Find the equation in the form $S=a+bA$.

examples.solution_text:
a. Read two points on the drawn line: $(0,10)$ and $(10,50)$.
$\begin{aligned}b&=\frac{50-10}{10-0}\\&=4\end{aligned}$
Predicted sales increase by $\$4000$ for each additional $\$1000$ spent on advertising.

b. The line crosses the vertical axis at $10$, so $a=10$.
$S=10+4A$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.11cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{fitcolour}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\definecolor{annotationcolour}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[gridcolour,xstep=1,ystep=10] (0,0) grid (10,60);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.7,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,64);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {10,20,30,40,50,60} {\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\path (5,-9) node {Advertising spend ($\$1000$)};
\path (-1.5,30) node[rotate=90] {Sales ($\$1000$)};
\foreach \x/\y in {0/12,1/11,2/20,3/19,4/28,5/27,6/36,7/35,8/44,10/48} {\fill[black] (\x,\y) circle (1.8pt);}
\draw[fitcolour,thick] (0,10)--(10,50);
\draw[annotationcolour,dashed] (0,10)--(10,10)--(10,50);
\path (5,10) node[below,text=annotationcolour] {run $=10$};
\path (10,30) node[right,text=annotationcolour] {rise $=40$};
\fill[annotationcolour] (0,10) circle (2pt);
\fill[annotationcolour] (10,50) circle (2pt);
\path (0,10) node[above right,text=annotationcolour] {$(0,10)$};
\path (10,50) node[above left,text=annotationcolour] {$(10,50)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

